Roq had always considered himself lucky.  When he found an uncursed ring, he
put it on.  He reached the bones of a wizard on level 5, a wizard who had
given his wand of cold to a nymph.  Well, luckily enough, the ring protected
him from it's effects.  So he killed the nymph, and then had the bright idea
to wield a dagger in each hand, and throw them as well.  The wizard had a
Cloak of magic resistance, which he immediatly put on.  On the same level,
he found a throne, so he sat on it, and got a wish.  He got +3 greased SDSM,
and lo and behold, the CoMR wasn't cursed, so he took it off, put on the
SDSM, and was really feeling tough now.

He hit the mines, where he promptly thought his luck had run out.  His
oldest brother (Roq I, their parent's weren't very imaginative) had died
here, with a pet Jabberwock.  So Roq ran down the stairs, wondering if the
mythical mall he had heard of would help him.  Well, one shop had a magic
harp, and another had a blessed magic lamp.  So another wish was used, after
much though, for Boots of Speed.  He found a cool gray rock at the bottom of
the mines, and decided to head out.  On his way up, he played some music,
and Fred the Jabberwock followed him out.


Did sokobon, it had the "oR, so he left.  Found a magic whistle, which made
fred a lot easier to handle.  While looting a vault, he found himself in a
fortress, that had a lot of soldiers.  Killed everyone, and then dragged the
money up to the minetown priest.  Fred got him a quick refund, and then he
took the money to a another priest.  This was repeated a couple times
throught the game, getting Roq a -1 naked AC.  Suddenly, Roq heard that the
master wanted him back, so back he went.  Jumped on the master assasin from
above, and zapped him with this cool wand that made bugs stop moving.  The
MA died instantly.  Did some saccing, got crowned, and another point of
protection.  Roq was using a cool sword he had recieved earlier, named
Stormbringer.  he was also given a very cold long sword, but for some reason
he couldn't bring himself to let the bloodthirsty blade be sheathed.  He did
decided to use both Stormbringer and a silver dagger that he had somehow
created at the fort, using a magical stick.  Found a couple magic markers,
was gifted a blank spellbook, so Roq decided to try to take his extensive
knowledge of the ?oID and write a book about it.  Pretty soon, he was
looking everywhere for loot.  (He ascended with quite a load of booty).  He
had learned how to fly for a short time, so he killed medusa, and then
cleaned out the castle.  Sat on the castle throne, and got another wish, so
he asked for a bag of holding.  he also found a helm of brilliance and
GoDex, and a shirt earlier, so by the time he found the castle's 0:3 wand,
he already had a full AK, a couple MM, and a ?oCharging.  Reverse genocided
nurses a couple times, wished up a few more MM's.  Recharged the wand and
didn't use it again.  Fully enchanted his armor and weapons, hit Gehennom,
Gehennom didn't hit back much.  Serously, Stormbringer and a silver dagger
were pretty good.  Most demons didn't last more than a hit or two, even the
dreaded arch-liches couldnt stand up to much.

Nothing to report in gehennom, polypiled rings and finally got a =oLev. (and
a =oFA as a side effect.)

Note my YASAD post, Orcus was almost the end of him.  I could see it now...
Roq IV, killed by a typo.

but anyway, the "oLS saved the day, and I continued on.

The wizard double troubled the High priest, but a wand of death solved the
wizards problems.  the high priest went down next (they hit HARD.  The only
time I ever dropped below 300HP was when I fought the High priest of Moloch,
and accidently pissed off the High Priest of Koa)


Flew out of gehennom, had two c!oGL, but didnt bother on the way out.

Flew through the dungeon, flew through earth, air, fire, water took a bit
longer, but not long compared to other ascensions.

Got to astral, hit pestelilence in the middle, but it was lawful.  Fought
back out, and killed death before he could hit me.  In fact, death NEVER
drained my life, he used touch of death once, every other time he died in
one round.  Stormbringer is ridiculously powerful.... I think....

